good morning ladies and gentlemen  welcome to the first press conference of  president from the line dedicated to the  readout of the first meeting of the  College of Commissioners President the  floor is yours thank you very much and a  very warm welcome from my side too  yes I want to report from the very first  college meeting which was for the very  first time a paperless College meeting  it was completely digital so it's a  first important step towards a digital  organization I know that as a whole we  have still a very very much to do but  having a paperless college is an  important first step I want to report on  what we've decided on today in the  college the working methods and then we  had reports on cop 25 in Madrid the hrbp  reported briefly from NATO the  Commission Elena church about Albania  was going to travel to today to be there  tomorrow and vice president Yoruba and  Commissioner winders reported from Malta  so first of all let's have a look at the  working methods we have been deciding on  today the Commission sees itself as one  team yes we do come from very different  backgrounds and different countries we  have different political colors but we  work as one College for one union and  this is our European Union we have all  our say in the college we decide  together and it is important that when  we have taken a decision we also thereby  take ownership all of us  this subject as it has been decided in  the college I emphasize this because we  always say that Europe is strong when it  is united and when it acts as one so if  the unity has to start here at the core  of the European institutions in the  college we have organized the work of  the Commission in such that if you look  at my six priorities and the guidelines  they are of course all interconnected  for example climate and digital have a  strong interconnection for an economic  growth strategy but we organized it as  such that an executive vice president or  a vice president is responsible for a  cluster with different commissioners we  call them commissioners group and they  are shared by the respective  vice-president or executive  vice-president or HR VP these  commissioners groups will ensure  coordination and coherence across the  Commission but the decisions of course  are being taken in the college we have  been taken a decision on the  geopolitical commission of course the  HIV people will support me in  coordinating the external dimension of  all commissioners work our external  action will be systematically discussed  and decided on by the college that was a  reason for example that today we had the  NATO report we will have every Wednesday  in college now a report on external  action and we have created a new  preparatory body the so-called xqo  external coordination that brings  together the cabinet's of all  commissioners to bridge mainly the  action that is external and internal  because both have a strong influence on  the Commission's work a few more topics  on the composition of our cabinet as you  know I've asked to include at least 50  sent women in all our cabinets at  administrative level we've reached that  goal for the very first time this is a  little revolution I'm proud of that at  the same time it should be normal it  should not be an issue and we've asked  to bring as many nationalities as  possible to the respective cabinets I'm  proud to say that we have in my cabinet  16 different nationalities and I've  encouraged my colleagues to raise the  numbers of nationalities in their teams  - last but not least an information on  the think-tank on the current European  political strategy center we will build  a new structure it is structured by the  six headlines of the political  guidelines or represented by the VP's I  want to keep the Femmes function of an  internal think tank at the same time I  want to adapt it to a new geopolitical  reality and to our new priorities we'll  call it ideal the acronym as always it's  an acronym for inspired debate engage  and accelerate action just a short  report on the cup 25 in Madrid first of  all I want to commend Spain for an  outstanding work and putting up with in  three weeks this huge conference this  was impressive I think it was very good  that I was there on my very first  working day on Monday to contribute to  making the European Green Deal a  reference for climate action I announced  that we will adopt the European Green  Deal  in the communication kind of a roadmap  next week on December 11th and presented  a few short ideas  within the three minutes we all did have  for our contributions the first one is  that I'm convinced only what gets  measured gets done and therefore we  announced at the cup 25 that in 2020 we  will have the first ever climate law in  place so that our road towards climate  neutrality in 2050 will be irreversible  the second point is investment  investment will be crucial to be  successful with the European Green Deal  for that we will present the sustainable  Europe and vestment plan to mobilize  investment and as you know the just  transition fund to leave no one behind  we make very clear that we want to be  ambitious in the negotiations and the  cop 25 I think the European Green Deal  could be seen as a real contribution to  something like a global Green Deal it  was good to see that all the European  leaders President Susilo was there and  president Michele was there too more or  less increasingly aligning on the  European Green Deal so it's going in the  right direction what our continent is  concerned but of course the cup 25 is a  vast international one impressive is  that we have the shared view that Europe  can be and must be a front-runner in  this topic but obviously they are also  concerned how we gonna finance that  mainly the transition and it is true  that we do not all start from the same  point and that is why we put forward the  just transition fund I want to inform  you that we are working towards an  aspirational target of mobilizing under  the Justin  mechanism together with the eiv group  100 billion euros of investments during  the period of the next mff in order to  reach that target we're building a  mechanism that draws and sources of  funding from the EU budget from the  European Union but also co-founded by  the Member States as well as the EIB  group to leverage the necessary public  and private means at the same time and I  think this is important too when we're  talking about costs of the European  Green Deal at the same time we should  always keep in mind what the cost of  non-action would be and there are costs  already so I asked the Commissioner  septa coverage of foresight to present  us next week the known costs already for  the European Union of climate change so  that we have an idea what the costs of  non-action would be in the future and  that we know all aligned in the being  convinced that acting on the Green Deal  is a good investment than the right  investment for a better future in a  healthy planet I'm convinced that this  is yes the European Green Deal fighting  climate change change it is not only  necessary is it it is a huge opportunity  for the European Union we are at the  moment being the front-runner if we do  it right if we invest in research and  innovation in green technologies  sustainable solutions and new businesses  we will be able to demonstrate as a  trendsetter  that this can be for the European Union  a new growth strategy and at the same  time if we make the transition we're  able to give people confidence we are  able to give the economy confidence  and hope that this is moving in the  right direction change of topic  Albania the European Union and I had a  phone call with Prime Minister Atacama  on Sunday stands in full solidarity with  Albania with actions not only with words  we support already on the ground we are  committed to providing more so far the  Commission has helped to mobilize three  search-and-rescue teams of more than 200  staff from Italy Greece and Romania  we've dispatched tens beds blankets  sleeping bags generators and hygiene  items for emergency needs by a Belgium  Romania Austria and Slovakia  Commissioner lenarcik will travel today  to Albania he is there mainly to provide  a cute assessment for the state the  buildings are in that are affected and  of course to have an primary assessment  on what kind of help is needed for  reconstruction as a very first step we  will allocate from the neighborhood fund  15 million immediately to support the  Albanian people and we've decided in  college that we will organize a donors  conference I will call today at Irama  again to inform him about these effects  last topic in the college meeting was  Malta I am concerned by the recent  developments in Malta and we are  following the situation very closely to  be very clear on that we harshly condemn  the murder of the journalist Daphne her  murder was an attack on free media  Media freedom is the foundation of our  free and democratic society journalists  must feel safe to work in Europe if not  democracy as we know it will be under  threat I will not comment on ongoing  national investigations however what I  will say is that I expect there to be a  thorough and independent investigation  free from any political interference  Europol is in Malta it is providing  support to the Maltese authorities it is  crucial that all those responsible are  brought to justice as soon as possible  the Commission is also in contact with  the Maltese authorities on the reform of  the judicial system and we will continue  to work with the authorities to  accelerate these reforms this is it for  the moment what  thank you mrs. president now the  president will now take your questions  and focusing first on the issues  discussed in the college as she  presented them yes
 

